{
    "background_story": "Sparky was a small but fierce terrier who lived in the Ottoman Empire during the 16th century. Despite his humble size, he had a big personality and a strong sense of loyalty. One day, he wandered into the barracks of the elite Janissary corps, an elite infantry unit known for their bravery and discipline. The soldiers were charmed by Sparky's bold spirit and decided to make him their mascot. As the Janissaries marched into battle, Sparky would trot alongside them, his tiny legs moving swiftly to keep up. He became a symbol of the corps' courage and tenacity, and his presence was said to bring good luck to the troops. Sparky's adventures with the Janissaries took him to the farthest reaches of the empire, earning him a legendary status as a loyal and trusted companion.",
